{
  "id": 516202990,
  "iid": 26081,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "radiotap: further improve 0-len PSDU display",
  "description": "Radiotap went through a bit of a strange iteration here: at\nthe start, 0-len PSDU was just that, for sounding packets,\nbut then other reasons to not have captured a PSDU came up\nand we added them there. This made the \"0-len\" be a misnomer,\nit can now represent a captured PLCP header for a real non-\nsounding PPDU, which isn't a zero-length PSDU.\n\nThe version of the improvement I sent a pull request for\nearlier made this, in a sense, even worse, because now the\nInfo column will always show \"0-len PSDU\", and while that's\nwhat the field is called in radiotap, I found that it really\nconfuses actual users in the field.\n\nSo make this a bit more descriptive:\n - show sounding PPDUs as such (\"sounding PPDU\")\n - show PPDUs with out PSDU as\n   - \"PSDU not captured\" for \"not captured\" in radiotap, and\n   - \"PSDU not captured (...)\" for other reasons\n - add the L-SIG length (which is zero for sounding PPDUs)\n   to the Info column as well, if available\n\nThis should clear up confusion, in particular \"0-len PSDU\"\ncases where the capture just ran into an error will now most\nlikely show as something like\n\n\tPSDU not captured (vendor-specific), L-SIG length 246\n\nwhich is much better than \"0-len PSDU (vendor-specific)\" for\nthis and similar cases.\n\nI've not touched the radiotap fields to keep existing filters\nworking as-is, I think it'd be wrong to change that now.",
